WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.329 --> 00:00:04.500
Blue Bloods fans were stunned earlier this
fall when the show unceremoniously killed

00:00:04.500 --> 00:00:09.030
off one of its main characters, especially
since the actress had touted the show just

00:00:09.030 --> 00:00:09.840
months before.

00:00:09.960 --> 00:00:14.520
"Seven seasons later, we're as strong as we've
ever been."

00:00:14.720 --> 00:00:17.860
As it turns out, the cast was reeling just
as much as everyone else.

00:00:18.100 --> 00:00:23.140
The show's actors recently spoke out on the
departure of Amy Carlson, whose Linda Reagan

00:00:23.150 --> 00:00:27.789
was revealed to be dead in the season 8 premiere,
revealing their shock and disappointment with

00:00:27.789 --> 00:00:29.280
the character's abrupt demise.

00:00:29.300 --> 00:00:33.480
Linda died off screen, with the show revealing
in its return that her character had been

00:00:33.480 --> 00:00:35.960
killed in a helicopter crash months earlier.

00:00:35.960 --> 00:00:40.240
After her exit, Carlson wrote a note of thanks
for fans who'd supported her throughout the

00:00:40.240 --> 00:00:40.740
series.

00:00:40.960 --> 00:00:45.000
Although she said she was grateful to the
cast and crew, Deadline reports that there

00:00:45.000 --> 00:00:49.580
may have been some trouble behind the scenes,
with Carlson reportedly deciding it was, quote,

00:00:49.580 --> 00:00:52.280
"time to move on" after fulfilling her contract.

00:00:52.410 --> 00:00:57.400
While Linda's death was hard on fans, it was
also especially hard on the character's husband,

00:00:57.400 --> 00:00:59.071
Danny, played by Donnie Wahlberg.

00:00:59.200 --> 00:01:03.600
Wahlberg said he didn't have to stray far
from the truth to play the grieving widower.

00:01:03.600 --> 00:01:07.780
He told the crowd at Paleyfest in New York,
"Rather than try to act or find something

00:01:07.780 --> 00:01:10.420
to do, I just thought about my friend Amy
Carlson.

00:01:10.560 --> 00:01:14.470
I thought about all the years together and
all the highs and lows and the ups and downs

00:01:14.470 --> 00:01:15.080
and the journey.

00:01:15.280 --> 00:01:19.220
Any tears I shed in that scene was really
Donnie shedding them for Amy…

00:01:19.220 --> 00:01:23.890
Hopefully this family of our cast, the show,
and the viewers will all mourn the loss together

00:01:23.890 --> 00:01:25.970
and move forward after this season."

00:01:25.970 --> 00:01:30.910
Some of Wahlberg's other co-stars also expressed
their sadness at Carlson's decision to leave

00:01:30.910 --> 00:01:31.410
the show.

00:01:31.640 --> 00:01:35.620
Sami Gayle told TVLine, "Amy made the decision
to leave, but we adore her....

00:01:35.620 --> 00:01:36.820
We're very sad she left."

00:01:37.020 --> 00:01:42.110
Marisa Ramirez, who plays Danny's partner
Detective Maria Baez, thinks the departure

00:01:42.110 --> 00:01:46.080
will prove interesting for the show because
Danny will now need to turn to her support,

00:01:46.080 --> 00:01:49.610
adding, "...we'll see if he takes it, because
he's very, very stubborn."

00:01:50.200 --> 00:01:54.560
Meanwhile, her co-star Bridget Moynahan added
that she was "disappointed" to learn that

00:01:54.560 --> 00:01:58.960
the actress was departing, saying, "It was
unfortunate that she made that decision at

00:01:58.960 --> 00:02:02.940
the end of Season 7, so we were stuck with
the storyline as we could get it.

00:02:03.040 --> 00:02:06.780
But I'm really thrilled for her to go off
and pursue other things and follow what she

00:02:06.780 --> 00:02:08.000
felt was best for her."

00:02:08.200 --> 00:02:12.450
Carlson, for her part, wrote on Twitter that
she was "appalled and sad" about the comments

00:02:12.450 --> 00:02:16.520
made at PaleyFest, saying, "I [love] the show,
cast and playing her."

00:02:18.260 --> 00:02:19.360
"Why are ya'll looking at me?"

00:02:20.100 --> 00:02:20.920
Thanks for watching!

